---
title: Strawberry Sode
source: direct-input
servings: 12
---

Prepare the @strawberries{2%lbs}(very ripe, hulled and sliced).

Quarter the strawberries (or cut into 6-8 pieces if they are very large) and place them in a #heavy-bottomed saucepan{}.

Pour in enough fresh cold @water{3%cups} to just cover the strawberries.

Place the saucepan over high heat and bring to a boil.

Once boiling, reduce the heat to low (or just above low) to maintain a gentle simmer.

Simmer uncovered for ~{15%minutes}. The strawberries will become very soft and pale as they release their color and flavor into the liquid.

Place a fine-mesh strainer over another saucepan.

Carefully ladle the cooked strawberry mixture into the strainer.

Allow the liquid to drain through completely without pressing on the pulp (this keeps the syrup clear). Discard the pulp.

Add @sugar{2%cups}(white granulated) to the strained strawberry liquid.

Stir and place the saucepan over high heat. Bring to a boil.

Once boiling, reduce heat to medium and cook for exactly ~{5%minutes}. You can skim off any foam that forms (optional).

After 5 minutes, turn off the heat and let the syrup cool completely.

Once cool, transfer the syrup to a clean jar or bottle. It is now ready to use.

Fill a tall glass with ice.

Add strawberry syrup to fill the glass between @?half{} and @?two-thirds{} full.

Top off the glass with @club soda{}.

Stir gently and enjoy.